messages:
alex_sales: Hey team — midmarket POC hit a blocker. Demo tomorrow; customer sends full conversation + attachments and we get "request body too big". They say ~60k tokens in prep. Any fast mitigation?

marta_se: Oof. Which model are they using and are we getting a 413 or a model error?

alex_sales: Using rdx-3b-long for the POC. Gateway returns "RequestEntityTooLarge" from our ingress, then the client sees a generic error. No app-level model response.

toni_support: Quick checks: 1) Are they doing JSON with large base64 attachments? 2) Is any proxy (nginx/ingress) imposing client_max_body_size?

eng_ben: Also check tokenization. 60k tokens -> payload huge. If it's conversation + attachments, consider stripping or uploading attachments to S3 and sending a link.

alex_sales: They are embedding files inline as base64. Can we accept links instead for the demo? Customer wants an offline proof where we process everything in one request.

toni_support: For demo quick-fix: (a) advise them to attach links instead of base64, (b) send only recent N turns (e.g., last 8) + summary of prior context, or (c) use streaming/chunked approach where you send smaller batches and keep state on server between calls.

eng_ben: If they absolutely need full convo in one shot, route them to a dedicated instance with bumped body limit and larger model context (rdx-8k or 32k). But that needs infra approval and will take hours.

infra_bot: deploy-note: cannot increase global front-door max request size without infra change. Temporary per-team reverse-proxy tweak possible but requires ops approval.

marta_se: For the immediate demo, propose we do a two-step POC: 1) Precompute a brief conversation summary (we can provide a tiny summarizer tool snippet) and send summary + last N turns. 2) In parallel, we offer a follow-up run on a dedicated endpoint for the entire archive as a stretch.

alex_sales: Client ok with summary approach if we give a sample summarizer they can run quickly. Can someone share a snippet?

eng_ben: Sharing quick Node snippet for summary — run locally on their machine to condense history:

```js
// pseudo: compress convo to summary + keep last 8 turns
const compress = (messages) => {
  const tail = messages.slice(-8);
  const prior = messages.slice(0, -8).join('
');
  // call a short summarization model or heuristic
  const summary = shortSummary(prior);
  return { summary, tail };
};
```

eng_ben: If they want us to host a tiny summarizer endpoint we can spin something ephemeral and avoid changing their client.

carl_emp: FYI price note — if we move them to dedicated for the full-run, the cost estimate doubles for GPU time. Mentioned for the customer so expectations are set.

toni_support: Also reminder: check their Content-Type headers. Some clients set incorrect boundaries for multipart which inflates payload.

alex_sales: Great. I'll propose summary + last N turns for the demo and offer a paid dedicated run afterwards. Can someone DM me the summarizer snippet and an ops contact for temporary proxy raise if needed?

marta_se: DM incoming. Also cc'ing @carl_emp so sales is aware on pricing. :+1:

infra_bot: ops-contact: @ops_oncall (pager). Raising a temp proxy permit will take ~3h and requires justification.

alex_sales: Thanks all — moving to action. Will update in thread after customer response. :v:
